Z||000001||KRMFiero||12-15-2000||03:10 PM||||Yes, they are good.... But For the price I would not pay it... they are VERY expensive.<P>Cheak out this forum:<P> <A HREF="http://www.termpro.com/cgi-bin/ubb/ultimate.cgi" TARGET=_blank>http://www.termpro.com/cgi-bin/ubb/ultimate.cgi</A> <P>very helpful, also the subs and encloser part   is very helpful in finding good quility subs.<P><BR>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||12-15-2000||05:31 PM||||I have three Rockford Fosgate Punch series power amps and they are awesome. I agree with KRM, the head units are good, but for a cheaper price, you can get an equally good unit. The mid to upper price range Pioneer units are some of the best CD players for NOT skipping. True, an Alpine might have a little better specs, but they are also known skippers. I don't know how well the R-F head units do on bumps, anyone else heard?||||reg||1
Z||000003||gkozlov||12-15-2000||08:10 PM||||I’ve never used the Fosgate head units, but I love their amps. My Punch 40 is a powerful amp. I use it to push my Kicker 10".<BR>I disagree with Batboy about Alpines skipping. I have an Alpine head unit and it has never skipped.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||pHoOl||12-15-2000||09:02 PM||||The RF unit that i was looking at was i believe around $220 before my friend's employee discount.  I'd like to get it for cheaper than that, but i guess that he'll get it for 5% more than the store pays for it.  So, now comes the question again of what i should do.  <P>Get the RF, or find a Pioneer for the same price.  Something that is kinda silly but almost a requirement is for it to glow red.  I want to keep the stock look, but i can't afford 300 for a used Pontiac Delco CD player.  Are there any pioneers that glow red?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
