Z||000007||onfire||12-16-2000||03:27 AM||||I have a Rockford Fosgate rfx 8320 and the rfx mp3.8 mediacard changer, in my truck. The cd player has never skipped on me yet, and I have gone over some pretty good potholes. The mp3.8 will never skip because it uses memory cards for the music. Boy are those things expensive.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I might have to get a different mp3 player for my truck.  <IMG SRC="http://rockets2.rockfordcorp.com/intershoproot/eCS/Store/en/Products/SourceUnits/images/prod_rfx8320.gif"> <BR>As you can see it doesn't have any red lights though. If you go with the 8340 or the 8350 there is some red in them.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://rockets2.rockfordcorp.com/intershoproot/eCS/Store/en/Products/SourceUnits/images/prod_rfx8340.gif">  <BR>Here is there website. <A HREF="http://www.rockfordfosgate.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rockfordfosgate.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>"I seen it on the internet, and I believe everthing on the net."<BR><A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank>Check out my waist of banbwidth.</A><p>[This message has been edited by onfire (edited 12-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||onfire||12-16-2000||03:35 AM||||I was wondering if anyone here has the Aiwa CDC-mp3 car stereo. And what there thoughts on it were. I was looking into one of those before I bought the RFXmp3.8. I just liked the idea of the music on the memory cards never skipping, when I'm out four wheeling. All those rough trails, and no radio reception. What other mp3 car stereos are out now besides what's mentioned and the overpriced Kenwood 919.||||reg||1
