Z||000011||KRMFiero||12-17-2000||10:00 PM||||the Aiwa pretty nice, feels cheap though... I reccomend a Pieneer,     If you guys want to be able to play MP3's in your car, get a Head unit with a input and get some old computer parts (100mhz, 16mb ram, 1 gb hdd, sound card and network card) and build yourself a MP3 player.. run windows have it autoload winamp and just get a keypad to change songs.... have the eathernet card to connect the computer to your home computer to load songs....    computers are 12 volts <P>well hope that helps something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Kyle ||||reg||10
Z||000012||pHoOl||12-18-2000||02:56 AM||||I have thought about that idea of building a computer and hooking it up.  Haven't completely designed it yet, and doubt i could fit it in a fiero.  but maybe with a little time (three weeks off from school) i could figure out something.  i was thinking of having a monitor though so that you could fully load whatever song you wanted and also do visualizations.<P>big problem is that the smallest monitor you can get is 5" i think and costs quite a chunk of change.<P>I think that i had a good design though, i was going to have the operating system load from a CD.  hopefully eliminating a hard drive in the process, just have two CDroms, one for the OS and one for the MP3z.  Sorry, computers are kinda my thing.  biggest part would be finding a power supply and case.  i pretty much have the rest of the parts. and if i did it without a monitor, i could probably get it to fit on top of the spare tire.<P>okay, now you got me thinking... good job... this is what i'll be doing all vacation.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
